# ---- Local working notes — never committed ----
CLAUDE.md

# ---- Vendored / fetched dependencies ----
# extern/ holds DolRecomp, SDL3, volk, VMA, spdlog and anything else pulled in
# from upstream. These are separate git repositories with their own history and
# their own licences; they are fetched or submoduled, never vendored into this
# repository's history.
extern/
third_party/
vendor/

# ---- Editor / OS ----
# .vscode/ IS TRACKED and is deliberately absent from this file. It carries the
# reasoning for why the vendored git repositories under extern/ are hidden from
# Source Control, and the git.ignoredRepositories list that does the hiding.
# That list is shared project configuration, not personal state.
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# ---- Game code and assets — LEGAL, not tidiness ----
# Nothing derived from the disc enters this repository. The user supplies their
# own images; the build hashes them and refuses anything else. No DOL, no REL,
# no generated C, no extracted assets or textures.
*.iso
*.gcm
*.rvz
*.nkit
*.nkit.iso
*.dol
*.rel
*.thp
*.dsp
*.adp
*.brstm
*.gcz
*.ciso
discs/
assets/
extracted/

# ---- Recompiler output ----
# DolRecomp emits 50-150 MB of C per DOL into build/generated/. It is a build
# artefact, regenerated from the user's own disc every build, and never edited.
build/
generated/

# ---- Symbol / analysis working files ----
# The recovered symbol map under config/symbols/ IS committed — it is our own
# naming work. Ghidra project state is not.
*.gpr
*.rep/
ghidra_*/
*.gzf

# ---- Native build output ----
cmake-build-*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeUserPresets.json
compile_commands.json
install_manifest.txt
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
*.dll
*.dylib
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.obj
*.lib
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log
build.ninja
rules.ninja

# ---- Shader / runtime caches and logs ----
shadercache/
*.spv
*.log
# ...but analysis logs ARE evidence and must be committed. They record what the
# analyser actually did, which is half the value of docs/evidence/. The blanket
# *.log above was silently swallowing them.
!docs/evidence/*.log
osreport-*.txt
frames/
saves/
memcard/

# ---- Python bytecode from tools/ ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The recompiled module, and anywhere a player is told to put it.
# GENERATED FROM THE PLAYER'S OWN DISC, so it is game-derived code and must
# never be committed - that is project rule 8, and it is what lets the
# executable be distributed at all. Saves are the player's data and are
# likewise theirs, not ours.
module/
*_recomp.so
# ...but not our own source directory of that name. game/module/ holds the
# glue that builds the module - our code, no game code - and a new file there
# (mgs_cpu.h) was silently ignored by the rule above. The built module is
# still kept out by *_recomp.so.
!/game/module/
